codemap 9
tour feature-step-link
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note step-link <name> <index> <target>: mark one step as the call site of the tour named target, so a reader follows the link instead of reading the shared code's steps again in every tour that reaches it. The agent needs it so shared code is mapped once in its own tour and every tour reaching it points there instead of copying its steps. index is the step index tours prints. An empty target is refused: step-unlink is the one way to remove a link. The target must exist and cannot be the step's own tour; tour --inline prints the linked tour inline under the step.

